{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-07): OPTION B — the anti-drift guard, not the glob.\n\nThe sweep's file list stays scoped to the transport layer as ticket 8a5e ruled correct. Add a guard that catches the drift case — a classified name being renamed or moved out from under the sweep — rather than widening the sweep's subject.\n\nRejected: the glob option. Measurement made the cost concrete: it pulls 90 new members across 8 modules into scope, each requiring individual mutating/non-mutating classification against the 429 policy, and it silently redefines what the sweep is ABOUT — from 'the transport layer' to 'the whole package' — contradicting 8a5e. That is a large classification effort in exchange for widening a boundary someone deliberately drew.\n\nSupporting measurement for B being sufficient today: scanning all 8 unswept modules for names already in `_CLASSIFIED_MUTATING` yields exactly 2 defs in 1 module, both known-benign delegations. So B is green now and its job is to stay that way.\n\nConsequence to handle in the same change: AC3 as literally worded is satisfied by the glob option but NOT by B. Rewrite AC3 to state what B actually guarantees — drift detection over the declared transport surface — rather than leaving a criterion that this decision cannot satisfy. (Per the operator's standing ruling: an unmeetable criterion is a defect in the criterion, to be remediated before close.)\n\nNote the ticket's own scope section lists `scripts/canary_bridge.py` but omits `acli_subprocess.py` and `jira_fields.py`, the latter named by the test's own docstring as one of the four 429 behaviours. Reconcile that list while implementing."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786115002992320001,"uuid":"fc5afb93-da9c-48ba-8a37-f1fc2cdb447d"}